[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid="uid://c8teibi001"]

; TEIBI, SKINNED — bead godot-test1-5u3.3, the first hero in this game on a
; Skeleton3D. One mesh on MPFB2's `game_engine` rig, 23 bones after
; `build_hero.cut_fingers()`, built by `scripts/build_hero.py teibi` (the source
; of record; `assets/models/characters/PROVENANCE.md` carries the row). The ten
; generated parts this scene used to instance, and the generator that wrote
; them, are retired with this bead.
;
; THE SCENE IS THE FLAG. Nothing in `scripts/` names Teibi to pose him: the
; Skeleton3D under `Body` is what makes `hero_rig.gd` hand him to
; `hero_rig_skeleton.gd` instead of `hero_rig_limbs.gd` (bd 5u3.2), which is why
; this migration is a data change and `player_animation.gd`,
; `remote_avatar.gd` and `player_abilities.gd` change by zero lines.
;
; THE UID IS LOAD-BEARING and stays `uid://c8teibi001`: `player_controller.gd`'s
; CHARACTERS points at the PATH, but a changed uid makes Godot rewrite every
; reference that resolved this scene by uid, and warn while it does it.
;
; `Body` stays even though the mesh needs no wrapper: the landing squash writes
; Body.position.y, `capture_rest_pose()` reads Body.rotation and the caller
; writes the lean and sway there for BOTH rig kinds, so every hero scene in this
; game has one. The .glb instance carries NO basis — a SKINNED glTF is exported
; Y-up and placed by its own root node, so the Rx(-90) every UNRIGGED part scene
; applies would lay the hero on his face.

